menu "device_esp32_spi"

    config DEVICE_ESP32_SPI_SLOTS
        int "Chips per bus"
        default 4
        range 1 6
        help
          How many chips one SPI bus device holds at once (ATTACH beyond it is
          ERR_SPI_NO_SLOT). ESP-IDF takes at most 6 devices per controller.

    config DEVICE_ESP32_SPI_QUEUE_MAX
        int "Queued transfers per chip"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
          The largest queue_depth an ATTACH may ask for: the transactions a
          chip may have queued at once (QUEUE).

    config DEVICE_ESP32_SPI_BOUNCE_BYTES
        int "Bounce buffer (bytes)"
        default 64
        range 16 4096
        help
          A blocking transfer that writes, then reads, in one CS goes through
          this buffer: its tx and rx together are at most this long. A bus
          has two of them (sent and received bytes), 2x this in RAM.

endmenu
